 * <p>The original implementation accepted an external seed via a {@link Resource}
 * and called {@code SecureRandom#setSeed(byte[])} with that data.  Supplying a
 * predictable or attacker‑controlled seed weakens the randomness and can
 * lead to cryptographic compromise.  This patched version removes the use of
 * external seed data entirely, relies on the JVM‑provided seeding mechanism,
 * and falls back to a strong default algorithm when the configured one is not
 * available.</p>
